  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — an informal anglicism borrowed from English \"to rank,\" common in gaming, sports, and SEO/marketing contexts (e.g. *rankear en Google*, *rankear en el torneo*)",
    "Not in the RAE dictionary — colloquial/technical usage only, more common in Latin America than Spain",
    "No spelling changes needed: unlike -car verbs (c→qu), the k stays k before every vowel, so it conjugates fully regularly",
    "Past participle: *rankeado* (regular)",
    "Example: *Ese video rankea muy bien en YouTube* (That video ranks very well on YouTube)"
  ],
